{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJvuzx2LHQcmwK1kmF9GB2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"The output contract — a four-branch union (architecture §5).\n2\t\n3\t    HarnessOutput = RenderedAnswer | ClarificationNeeded | Unsupported | BudgetExceeded\n4\t\n5\tThe split between what the MODEL returns and what the HARNESS returns is the\n6\tload-bearing design here, and it comes straight out of M2's grader work:\n7\t\n8\t* `AnswerDraft` is what the model may author — the narrative, the question it\n9\t  answered, and its statement of what was missing or empty. It is one of the\n10\t  three branches in the agent's `output_type`.\n11\t* `RenderedAnswer` is what a caller receives. The harness builds it by attaching\n12\t  the six preserved contract fields **from the envelope the tool actually\n13\t  returned**, in code.\n14\t\n15\tThe reason is recorded in ADR-013: `limitations_verbatim` can prove the strings\n16\tsurvived intact, but nothing deterministic can prove a model did not paraphrase\n17\tthem on the way through. So the model never gets the chance — it does not carry\n18\tthose fields at all. The same argument covers `confidence` (ADR-009: the harness\n19\tdisplays what the data layer stated and never assigns a grade), `provenance`,\n20\tand `evidence`.\n21\t\n22\t`BudgetExceeded` is likewise never model-selectable: it is produced by the\n23\tcontrol envelope in `ask()` when a budget trips (ADR-004).\n24\t\"\"\"\n25\t\n26\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n27\t\n28\tfrom typing import Any, Literal, Union\n29\t\n30\tfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n31\t\n32\t\n33\tclass AnswerDraft(BaseModel):\n34\t    \"\"\"What the model returns when it can answer from the returned evidence.\n35\t\n36\t    Deliberately small. Everything the contract obliges the harness to preserve\n37\t    is attached afterwards from the envelope, so there is no field here a model\n38\t    could paraphrase, soften, or invent.\n39\t    \"\"\"\n40\t\n41\t    kind: Literal[\"answer\"] = \"answer\"\n42\t    question_id: str = Field(\n43\t        description=\"The registry question ID the evidence was fetched for.\"\n44\t    )\n45\t    answer: str = Field(\n46\t        description=(\n47\t            \"The narrative. Every number in it must appear in the returned \"\n48\t            \"evidence or in the user's own question.\"\n49\t        )\n50\t    )\n51\t    data_status_note: str = Field(\n52\t        default=\"\",\n53\t        description=(\n54\t            \"What came back empty or gappy, stated plainly at the point the \"\n55\t            \"number would have been. Empty string when the series is complete.\"\n56\t        ),\n57\t    )\n58\t\n59\t\n60\tclass ClarificationNeeded(BaseModel):\n61\t    \"\"\"A material input is missing and must not be invented (architecture §7).\"\"\"\n62\t\n63\t    kind: Literal[\"clarification\"] = \"clarification\"\n64\t    question_id: str = Field(\n65\t        description=\"The registry question this would map to, tentatively.\"\n66\t    )\n67\t    missing: list[\"MissingInput\"] = Field(\n68\t        description=\"The material inputs the user has to supply. Never empty.\"\n69\t    )\n70\t    prompt_to_user: str = Field(description=\"The question to put to the user.\")\n71\t\n72\t\n73\tclass MissingInput(BaseModel):\n74\t    input: str = Field(description=\"The request field name, as the contract names it.\")\n75\t    why_material: str = Field(\n76\t        description=\"Why this cannot be defaulted — one sentence, in the user's terms.\"\n77\t    )\n78\t    allowed_values: list[str] = Field(\n79\t        default_factory=list,\n80\t        description=\"Allow-listed values from the input catalog, when the field has them.\",\n81\t    )\n82\t\n83\t\n84\tclass Unsupported(BaseModel):\n85\t    \"\"\"The honest refusal. `reason` is CONTRACT TEXT, not harness prose (ADR-009).\n86\t\n87\t    `not_yet_validated` is the v0.3.0 case of a registered capability awaiting a\n88\t    passing backtest (VC-POC-14); it must never be rendered as \"we do not answer\n89\t    that\". `unanswerable` is the v0.3.0 abstention for a valid, registered\n90\t    request whose required fact is absent for the given inputs — distinct from a\n91\t    contract exclusion and from an empty result.\n92\t    \"\"\"\n93\t\n94\t    kind: Literal[\"unsupported\"] = \"unsupported\"\n95\t    reason_kind: Literal[\n96\t        \"excluded_by_contract\",\n97\t        \"not_in_registry\",\n98\t        \"out_of_scope\",\n99\t        \"not_yet_validated\",\n100\t        \"unanswerable\",\n101\t    ]\n102\t    reason: str = Field(\n103\t        description=(\n104\t            \"For a contract exclusion, the exclusion text itself, copied verbatim \"\n105\t            \"from the registry or the emitter's error envelope.\"\n106\t        )\n107\t    )\n108\t    reason_code: str | None = Field(\n109\t        default=None,\n110\t        description=(\n111\t            \"The registry-owned refusal reason code (v0.3.0), attached by the harness \"\n112\t            \"when the data layer excludes a registered question — e.g. deferred_capability \"\n113\t            \"or not_yet_validated. None for a model-authored refusal or a non-exclusion abstention.\"\n114\t        ),\n115\t    )\n116\t    nearest_supported: str | None = Field(\n117\t        default=None, description=\"A registry question ID that CAN be answered, if one is close.\"\n118\t    )\n119\t\n120\t\n121\tclass RenderedAnswer(BaseModel):\n122\t    \"\"\"What a caller receives for an answered question.\n123\t\n124\t    The six preserved fields are attached by the harness from the envelope. A\n125\t    caller that renders this object is rendering the data layer's own words for\n126\t    limitations and confidence, by construction rather than by good behaviour.\n127\t    \"\"\"\n128\t\n129\t    kind: Literal[\"answer\"] = \"answer\"\n130\t    answer: str\n131\t    question_id: str\n132\t    contract_version: str\n133\t    evidence: list[dict[str, Any]]\n134\t    provenance: dict[str, Any]\n135\t    confidence: dict[str, Any]\n136\t    limitations: list[str]\n137\t    deterministic_signals: list[dict[str, Any]] = Field(default_factory=list)\n138\t    # v0.3.0 preserved fields, attached from the envelope in code (never authored\n139\t    # by the model): the resolved request the data layer actually ran, the\n140\t    # structured coverage of what came back, and the per-claim eligibility. The\n141\t    # five-grade label and its detail ride inside `confidence` as the data layer\n142\t    # stated them — the harness still assigns no grade of its own (ADR-009).\n143\t    resolved_request: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n144\t    data_status: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n145\t    claim_eligibility: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n146\t    data_status_note: str = \"\"\n147\t\n148\t    @classmethod\n149\t    def from_envelope(cls, draft: AnswerDraft, envelope: dict[str, Any]) -> RenderedAnswer:\n150\t        return cls(\n151\t            answer=draft.answer,\n152\t            question_id=envelope[\"question_id\"],\n153\t            contract_version=envelope[\"contract_version\"],\n154\t            evidence=envelope[\"evidence\"],\n155\t            provenance=envelope[\"provenance\"],\n156\t            confidence=envelope[\"confidence\"],\n157\t            limitations=envelope[\"limitations\"],\n158\t            deterministic_signals=envelope.get(\"deterministic_signals\", []),\n159\t            resolved_request=envelope.get(\"resolved_request\", {}),\n160\t            data_status=envelope.get(\"data_status\", {}),\n161\t            claim_eligibility=envelope.get(\"claim_eligibility\", {}),\n162\t            data_status_note=draft.data_status_note,\n163\t        )\n164\t\n165\t\n166\tclass BudgetExceeded(BaseModel):\n167\t    \"\"\"The control envelope tripped (ADR-004). A typed outcome, never a crash,\n168\t    and never selectable by the model.\"\"\"\n169\t\n170\t    kind: Literal[\"budget_exceeded\"] = \"budget_exceeded\"\n171\t    limit: Literal[\"steps\", \"tool_calls\", \"seconds\", \"usd\"]\n172\t    detail: str = \"\"\n173\t    learned_so_far: str = Field(\n174\t        default=\"\",\n175\t        description=\"What the run established before the budget tripped, if anything.\",\n176\t    )\n177\t\n178\t\n179\tClarificationNeeded.model_rebuild()\n180\t\n181\t# What the model may choose between.\n182\tAgentOutput = Union[AnswerDraft, ClarificationNeeded, Unsupported]\n183\t\n184\t# What `ask()` returns.\n185\tHarnessOutput = Union[RenderedAnswer, ClarificationNeeded, Unsupported, BudgetExceeded]\n186\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a5a4bf9-713c-4453-8836-6a3d15f3b2d0","uuid":"92ec685c-0d8a-4caa-b941-09e735c34c73","timestamp":"2026-09-25T22:59:11.558Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/harness/outputs.py","content":"\"\"\"The output contract — a four-branch union (architecture §5).\n\n    HarnessOutput = RenderedAnswer | ClarificationNeeded | Unsupported | BudgetExceeded\n\nThe split between what the MODEL returns and what the HARNESS returns is the\nload-bearing design here, and it comes straight out of M2's grader work:\n\n* `AnswerDraft` is what the model may author — the narrative, the question it\n  answered, and its statement of what was missing or empty. It is one of the\n  three branches in the agent's `output_type`.\n* `RenderedAnswer` is what a caller receives. The harness builds it by attaching\n  the six preserved contract fields **from the envelope the tool actually\n  returned**, in code.\n\nThe reason is recorded in ADR-013: `limitations_verbatim` can prove the strings\nsurvived intact, but nothing deterministic can prove a model did not paraphrase\nthem on the way through. So the model never gets the chance — it does not carry\nthose fields at all. The same argument covers `confidence` (ADR-009: the harness\ndisplays what the data layer stated and never assigns a grade), `provenance`,\nand `evidence`.\n\n`BudgetExceeded` is likewise never model-selectable: it is produced by the\ncontrol envelope in `ask()` when a budget trips (ADR-004).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Literal, Union\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\n\nclass AnswerDraft(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"What the model returns when it can answer from the returned evidence.\n\n    Deliberately small. Everything the contract obliges the harness to preserve\n    is attached afterwards from the envelope, so there is no field here a model\n    could paraphrase, soften, or invent.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    kind: Literal[\"answer\"] = \"answer\"\n    question_id: str = Field(\n        description=\"The registry question ID the evidence was fetched for.\"\n    )\n    answer: str = Field(\n        description=(\n            \"The narrative. Every number in it must appear in the returned \"\n            \"evidence or in the user's own question.\"\n        )\n    )\n    data_status_note: str = Field(\n        default=\"\",\n        description=(\n            \"What came back empty or gappy, stated plainly at the point the \"\n            \"number would have been. Empty string when the series is complete.\"\n        ),\n    )\n\n\nclass ClarificationNeeded(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"A material input is missing and must not be invented (architecture §7).\"\"\"\n\n    kind: Literal[\"clarification\"] = \"clarification\"\n    question_id: str = Field(\n        description=\"The registry question this would map to, tentatively.\"\n    )\n    missing: list[\"MissingInput\"] = Field(\n        description=\"The material inputs the user has to supply. Never empty.\"\n    )\n    prompt_to_user: str = Field(description=\"The question to put to the user.\")\n\n\nclass MissingInput(BaseModel):\n    input: str = Field(description=\"The request field name, as the contract names it.\")\n    why_material: str = Field(\n        description=\"Why this cannot be defaulted — one sentence, in the user's terms.\"\n    )\n    allowed_values: list[str] = Field(\n        default_factory=list,\n        description=\"Allow-listed values from the input catalog, when the field has them.\",\n    )\n\n\nclass Unsupported(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"The honest refusal. `reason` is CONTRACT TEXT, not harness prose (ADR-009).\n\n    `not_yet_validated` is the v0.3.0 case of a registered capability awaiting a\n    passing backtest (VC-POC-14); it must never be rendered as \"we do not answer\n    that\". `unanswerable` is the v0.3.0 abstention for a valid, registered\n    request whose required fact is absent for the given inputs — distinct from a\n    contract exclusion and from an empty result.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    kind: Literal[\"unsupported\"] = \"unsupported\"\n    reason_kind: Literal[\n        \"excluded_by_contract\",\n        \"not_in_registry\",\n        \"out_of_scope\",\n        \"not_yet_validated\",\n        \"unanswerable\",\n    ]\n    reason: str = Field(\n        description=(\n            \"For a contract exclusion, the exclusion text itself, copied verbatim \"\n            \"from the registry or the emitter's error envelope.\"\n        )\n    )\n    reason_code: str | None = Field(\n        default=None,\n        description=(\n            \"The registry-owned refusal reason code (v0.3.0), attached by the harness \"\n            \"when the data layer excludes a registered question — e.g. deferred_capability \"\n            \"or not_yet_validated. None for a model-authored refusal or a non-exclusion abstention.\"\n        ),\n    )\n    nearest_supported: str | None = Field(\n        default=None, description=\"A registry question ID that CAN be answered, if one is close.\"\n    )\n\n\nclass RenderedAnswer(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"What a caller receives for an answered question.\n\n    The six preserved fields are attached by the harness from the envelope. A\n    caller that renders this object is rendering the data layer's own words for\n    limitations and confidence, by construction rather than by good behaviour.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    kind: Literal[\"answer\"] = \"answer\"\n    answer: str\n    question_id: str\n    contract_version: str\n    evidence: list[dict[str, Any]]\n    provenance: dict[str, Any]\n    confidence: dict[str, Any]\n    limitations: list[str]\n    deterministic_signals: list[dict[str, Any]] = Field(default_factory=list)\n    # v0.3.0 preserved fields, attached from the envelope in code (never authored\n    # by the model): the resolved request the data layer actually ran, the\n    # structured coverage of what came back, and the per-claim eligibility. The\n    # five-grade label and its detail ride inside `confidence` as the data layer\n    # stated them — the harness still assigns no grade of its own (ADR-009).\n    resolved_request: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n    data_status: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n    claim_eligibility: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n    data_status_note: str = \"\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_envelope(cls, draft: AnswerDraft, envelope: dict[str, Any]) -> RenderedAnswer:\n        return cls(\n            answer=draft.answer,\n            question_id=envelope[\"question_id\"],\n            contract_version=envelope[\"contract_version\"],\n            evidence=envelope[\"evidence\"],\n            provenance=envelope[\"provenance\"],\n            confidence=envelope[\"confidence\"],\n            limitations=envelope[\"limitations\"],\n            deterministic_signals=envelope.get(\"deterministic_signals\", []),\n            resolved_request=envelope.get(\"resolved_request\", {}),\n            data_status=envelope.get(\"data_status\", {}),\n            claim_eligibility=envelope.get(\"claim_eligibility\", {}),\n            data_status_note=draft.data_status_note,\n        )\n\n\nclass BudgetExceeded(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"The control envelope tripped (ADR-004). A typed outcome, never a crash,\n    and never selectable by the model.\"\"\"\n\n    kind: Literal[\"budget_exceeded\"] = \"budget_exceeded\"\n    limit: Literal[\"steps\", \"tool_calls\", \"seconds\", \"usd\"]\n    detail: str = \"\"\n    learned_so_far: str = Field(\n        default=\"\",\n        description=\"What the run established before the budget tripped, if anything.\",\n    )\n\n\nClarificationNeeded.model_rebuild()\n\n# What the model may choose between.\nAgentOutput = Union[AnswerDraft, ClarificationNeeded, Unsupported]\n\n# What `ask()` returns.\nHarnessOutput = Union[RenderedAnswer, ClarificationNeeded, Unsupported, BudgetExceeded]\n","numLines":186,"startLine":1,"totalLines":186}}}
