{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfQzcb4wk1GnFNuJ9JWeS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Any` is already imported. The implementation is complete and self-consistent.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause found:** `evals/live.py` already parsed and validated a `--stage {intent,narration,end-to-end}` flag and recorded it in the checkpoint, but `run_trial`/`run_suite` never branched on it — every trial, regardless of `--stage`, ran the same legacy tool-loop (`build_agent()` + `ask(agent, deps, question)`). The flag was decorative.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`evals/live.py`** — Added three genuinely isolated trial runners: `run_intent_trial` (Stage 1 alone — `interpret_intent()`, no tools, no subprocess), `run_narration_trial` (Stage 4 alone — fetches the case's own declared envelope directly, builds an `AnswerView`, calls `narrate()`), and `run_end_to_end_trial` (drives the real new-pipeline `ask(deps, question)`, not the legacy signature). `run_trial`/`run_suite` now dispatch on `stage` to these (default `None` is unchanged legacy behaviour). Extracted the auth/quota-vs-failed-trial classification into a shared `_crashed_trial` helper so that rule can't drift between stages. `select_cases` now filters to cases with a fixed `expected_question_id`/`expected_request` for `--stage narration`. `main()` now passes `stage=args.stage` into `run_suite`. Checkpointing, resumability, `--max-trials` chunking, and completed-trial semantics (`completed_reports`, `aggregate`) were untouched.\n- **`evals/graders.py`** — Added `grade_intent`/`grade_intent_question_match` (isolated Stage-1 grading) and `NARRATION_GRADERS`/`grade_case_narration` (the full prose/envelope rule set minus the three graders that judge a decision narration never makes: question/request selection and school resolution).\n- **`tests/unit/test_live_tier.py`** — Added offline `FunctionModel`-scripted tests covering: isolation of the intent stage (no tool calls, correct/wrong/refusal classification, crash handling), isolation of the narration stage (grounded pass, ungrounded → harness gate rejection, cases with no fixed envelope are skipped, `select_cases` filtering), and the end-to-end stage running the real pipeline offline through the stub emitter with both stages scripted.\n- **`harness/answer_view.py`, `harness/intent.py`, `harness/narration.py`, `evals/replay.py`, `evals/schema.py`** — read for context; no changes were needed there (their existing single-call/no-tool contracts already supported isolated invocation).\n\n**Checks performed:** Read-through verification of type/field consistency (`RenderedAnswer` construction, `Deps`/`ToolInvocation`/`ToolCall` shapes, `StructuredIntent` fields, `spend_usd([])` semantics, pinned request-schema minimal payloads for `VC-POC-REF-01`) against the existing modules and other tests (`test_intent_boundary.py`, `test_planner.py`). I could not execute pytest in this environment, so these are static/read verifications, not a confirmed green run.\n\n**Unresolved / blocked:** The two work-item context files (`.../acceptance/001-contract.yaml` and `.../planning/001-plan.md`) were declared read-only inputs but the tool environment repeatedly refused permission to read them (not a user denial I could resolve), so this implementation was derived from the repository's own contract docs, `docs/decisions.md`, and the existing test suite as the best available specification. If the acceptance contract specifies different grading rules, CLI shapes, or stage semantics than what's implemented here, that should be reconciled against this diff."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":188361,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":428},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a5a4bf9-713c-4453-8836-6a3d15f3b2d0","uuid":"a96ebd2a-61c0-4047-bfde-43f75bf91f01","request_id":"req_011CfQzcaAcT2xAxEhALVE4g"}
